that ever happened to me.

00:01:18.896 --> 00:01:21.840
He is just everything.

00:01:21.840 --> 00:01:24.390
And, you know, I get so
emotional talking about it

00:01:24.390 --> 00:01:26.250
because I loved my children so much

00:01:26.250 --> 00:01:28.290
and I didn't know how it was going to be.

00:01:28.290 --> 00:01:30.600
- Yeah.
- And then he was here

00:01:30.600 --> 00:01:33.420
and I just cannot believe
it didn't happen sooner

00:01:33.420 --> 00:01:35.070
because it's the best thing.

00:01:35.070 --> 00:01:38.124
And he calls me Nanny Pinky.

00:01:38.124 --> 00:01:38.957
(audience laughing)

00:01:38.957 --> 00:01:40.410
- Nanny Pinky?
- Nanny Pinky.

00:01:40.410 --> 00:01:42.090
And all I wanted for Christmas,

00:01:42.090 --> 00:01:44.130
'cause he's just, you
know, starting speak,

00:01:44.130 --> 00:01:45.300
was to call me Nanny Pinky.

00:01:45.300 --> 00:01:47.587
And sure enough on Christmas Eve he said,

00:01:47.587 --> 00:01:48.990
"I love you Nanny Pinky,"

00:01:48.990 --> 00:01:51.660
and that was it, that was it.
- Like that's my gift.

00:01:51.660 --> 00:01:53.456
- I couldn't have asked for more,

00:01:53.456 --> 00:01:54.289
I couldn't have asked for-
- Oh, I love that.

00:01:54.289 --> 00:01:55.122
Well, the best part too

00:01:55.122 --> 00:01:58.410
is that you get to send
them home with your kid.

00:01:58.410 --> 00:02:00.480
I think that's why it's
so enjoyable (laughs).

00:02:00.480 --> 00:02:02.250
- It is, knowing you have that option,

00:02:02.250 --> 00:02:04.290
but I don't like sending him home.

00:02:04.290 --> 00:02:05.400
I love him.

00:02:05.400 --> 00:02:07.620
I mean, Pandora's very, very, you know,

00:02:07.620 --> 00:02:09.810
kind of hands-on mother.
- Yeah.

00:02:09.810 --> 00:02:12.300
- But it's no coincidence

00:02:12.300 --> 00:02:14.220
that I live a hundred yards
around the corner as well.

00:02:14.220 --> 00:02:15.300
- Oh, that's wonderful.

00:02:15.300 --> 00:02:17.477
- Yeah, maybe she doesn't
think so (laughs).

00:02:18.734 --> 00:02:19.567
- Who cares?

00:02:19.567 --> 00:02:20.730
Now you have a new restaurant

00:02:20.730 --> 00:02:22.080
and it's called Wolf, right?

00:02:22.080 --> 00:02:23.580
- Yes, I named it after him,

00:02:23.580 --> 00:02:25.950
his name is Teddy Wolf

00:02:25.950 --> 00:02:29.490
and it's opening in Lake
Tahoe in a couple of weeks,

00:02:29.490 --> 00:02:30.450
if ever I get back there

00:02:30.450 --> 00:02:32.220
and do what I'm supposed to be doing.

00:02:32.220 --> 00:02:33.053
But very-
- Teddy Wolf.

00:02:33.053 --> 00:02:34.830
- Yes, well it's just called Wolf,

00:02:34.830 --> 00:02:35.663
it's Wolf by-

00:02:35.663 --> 00:02:36.496
- No, I know, just that
he named Teddy Wolf,

00:02:36.496 --> 00:02:37.860
that's a very great name, yeah.

00:02:37.860 --> 00:02:39.600
- Well they talked about
his second name being Bear

00:02:39.600 --> 00:02:40.433
and I was like, no, no.

00:02:40.433 --> 00:02:42.000
If he's gonna be a
United States president,

00:02:42.000 --> 00:02:43.788
he cannot be called Teddy Bear, so.

00:02:43.788 --> 00:02:46.371
(all laughing)

00:02:48.354 --> 00:02:49.187
- [Kelly] I didn't think about that.

00:02:49.187 --> 00:02:50.730
- So yeah, the new
restaurant's called Wolf

00:02:50.730 --> 00:02:52.320
and it's exciting.

00:02:52.320 --> 00:02:54.240
With another one with Caesar's Palace.

00:02:54.240 --> 00:02:56.550
- Yeah, is this the third?

00:02:56.550 --> 00:02:58.500
- Third, and then I'm opening the fourth,

00:02:58.500 --> 00:02:59.550
which we named after me,

00:02:59.550 --> 00:03:00.930
Pinky, my nickname.
- Yeah.

00:03:00.930 --> 00:03:03.540
- And it would be Pinky's by
Vanderpump in the Flamingo.

00:03:03.540 --> 00:03:05.882
So yeah, it's so super, super busy.

00:03:05.882 --> 00:03:09.647
- [Kelly] That's amazing.
(audience cheering)

00:03:09.647 --> 00:03:13.920
- That's my restaurant in Paris Casino

00:03:13.920 --> 00:03:16.860
and we designed it in Caesar's.

00:03:16.860 --> 00:03:17.880
- Yeah.
- And it was just,

00:03:17.880 --> 00:03:21.150
I think voted like the 10th or 11th

00:03:21.150 --> 00:03:23.838
most photographed restaurant
in the United States, so.

00:03:23.838 --> 00:03:24.738
- That's so cool.
- Yeah.

00:03:24.738 --> 00:03:25.673
- You are so successful at it-
- Oh my God, look at you.

00:03:27.986 --> 00:03:29.034
- People love it so much.

00:03:29.034 --> 00:03:29.867
- Look at you.

00:03:29.867 --> 00:03:30.780
- No, I'm just saying like,

00:03:30.780 --> 00:03:31.980
what is it about Vegas?

00:03:31.980 --> 00:03:33.060
'Cause you keep opening your restaurant,

00:03:33.060 --> 00:03:35.190
they're wealth because you keep
making money at it probably.

00:03:35.190 --> 00:03:36.747
- No, no, but it's like it's Vegas

00:03:36.747 --> 00:03:40.770
and I think even more
so since the pandemic.

00:03:40.770 --> 00:03:42.930
You know, it was very
hard for restaurateurs

00:03:42.930 --> 00:03:45.300
and a hundred thousand, more than that,

00:03:45.300 --> 00:03:46.770
closed down in America.
- Yeah.

00:03:46.770 --> 00:03:48.840
- And my hat goes off to anybody

00:03:48.840 --> 00:03:50.430
that managed to keep their business afloat

00:03:50.430 --> 00:03:53.220
'cause it was really,
you know, a struggle.

00:03:53.220 --> 00:03:56.400
But I think Vegas is just so vibrant now

00:03:56.400 --> 00:03:58.259
and people really go there to play.

00:03:58.259 --> 00:03:59.760
- I love it, I go there
to do shows, it's fun

00:03:59.760 --> 00:04:00.593
because you go in and out.

00:04:00.593 --> 00:04:02.040
Yeah, yeah.
- Yeah.

00:04:02.040 --> 00:04:03.960
- Great food, good shows.
- I don't go in and out,

00:04:03.960 --> 00:04:04.980
I go and I stay there.

00:04:04.980 --> 00:04:06.630
I love it, yeah.

00:04:06.630 --> 00:04:07.920
- Oh, I'm usually in and out.

00:04:07.920 --> 00:04:09.300
I want a good meal, some great coffee,

00:04:09.300 --> 00:04:10.667
and I'll give a show (laughs).

00:04:12.120 --> 00:04:12.960
Do you love Vegas?

00:04:12.960 --> 00:04:13.793
Do you love going there?

00:04:13.793 --> 00:04:17.370
- I actually, we took my
mom for her 60th birthday.

00:04:17.370 --> 00:04:19.140
But what was hilarious was I was so tired

00:04:19.140 --> 00:04:20.490
'cause I had been shooting

00:04:20.490 --> 00:04:22.500
and someone bet me to ask for a hot,

00:04:22.500 --> 00:04:24.390
you know, they'd like do your
drink orders on the thing?

00:04:24.390 --> 00:04:25.223
- Yeah.
- Like someone said,

00:04:25.223 --> 00:04:26.940
"I'll give you 50 bucks if
you order a hot chocolate."

00:04:26.940 --> 00:04:28.260
I was like, "Okay."

00:04:28.260 --> 00:04:29.640
So there I was like betting cards

00:04:29.640 --> 00:04:30.473
and drinking my hot chocolate.

00:04:30.473 --> 00:04:32.242
- Oh, I see.
- Yeah, yeah.

00:04:32.242 --> 00:04:33.075
- It could have been worse,

00:04:33.075 --> 00:04:33.908
it could have been a cup of tea.

00:04:33.908 --> 00:04:34.741
- Yeah, exactly.

00:04:34.741 --> 00:04:36.850
- Yeah, throw some Amarula
in there, just saying.

00:04:36.850 --> 00:04:38.943
- Yeah.
- Yeah, it's a good day.

00:04:39.960 --> 00:04:42.030
So wait, so your new season
of "Vanderpump Rules,"

00:04:42.030 --> 00:04:42.990
like what's going on,

00:04:42.990 --> 00:04:43.823
what's a tease for us?

00:04:43.823 --> 00:04:45.960
- It was so complicated, you know,

00:04:45.960 --> 00:04:48.480
and it kind of blew up
out of the stratosphere.

00:04:48.480 --> 00:04:50.340
I mean, it was just so crazy.

00:04:50.340 --> 00:04:53.190
It was a lot of bad
behavior the season before.

00:04:53.190 --> 00:04:54.720
Yeah.
- And we tried to sort it out,

00:04:54.720 --> 00:04:57.090
but we'd stopped filming
when it was all exposed.

00:04:57.090 --> 00:04:58.710
So we need this season,

00:04:58.710 --> 00:05:01.230
this season feels very
different to any other season

00:05:01.230 --> 00:05:02.670
to sort it out.

00:05:02.670 --> 00:05:04.500
And as the kind of matriarch,

00:05:04.500 --> 00:05:05.430
do you ever watch the show?

00:05:05.430 --> 00:05:07.080
You're looking at me like maybe you do.

00:05:07.080 --> 00:05:10.284
- No, I'm just fascinated by
everything you do, I'm like.

00:05:10.284 --> 00:05:11.144
- Really?
- Yeah.

00:05:11.144 --> 00:05:12.120
- Like what don't you do?

00:05:12.120 --> 00:05:12.953
It's insane.

00:05:12.953 --> 00:05:15.044
- Oh, there's a couple of
things, ask my husband.

00:05:15.044 --> 00:05:18.192
(audience laughing and cheering)

00:05:18.192 --> 00:05:19.544
- Stop it.

00:05:19.544 --> 00:05:23.627
(audience laughing and cheering)

00:05:24.630 --> 00:05:25.880
- It's the British humor.

00:05:27.604 --> 00:05:30.493
- I have so many jokes.

00:05:30.493 --> 00:05:32.760
They're so wasted right now.

00:05:32.760 --> 00:05:35.010
God, I wish this was a nighttime show.

00:05:35.010 --> 00:05:36.750
Well, we need another
commercial break everybody.

